P. Ā. -णमति, ˚ते (aor. पर्य्-अणंसीत् ind.p. परि-णम्य), to bend or turn aside, AV.;
to bend down, stoop, Kāv.;
to change or be transformed into (instr.), Vedāntas.; Madhus.;
to develop, become ripe or mature, Bālar.;
to become old, Kir.;
to be digested, MBh.; Pañc.;
to be fulfilled (as a word), Pañc. :
Caus. -णामयति (ind.p. -णाम्य; Pass. -णाम्यते, p. णाम्यमान, or ˚म्यत्),
to make ripe, ripen, mature, ŚvetUp.;
to bring to an end, pass (as a night), R.;
to bend aside or down, stoop, MBh.

P. Ā. -णयति, ˚ते (pf. Ā. -णिन्ये, Daś.; -णयाम् आस, MBh.; 3. pl. aor. -अनेषत, RV.; ind.p. -णीय, Kum.),
to lead or bear or carry about or round, RV. &c. &c., (esp.) to lead a bride and bridegroom round the sacrificial fire (with 2 acc.)
to marry (said of a bridegroom), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to lead forward to, put or place anywhere (अग्रम्, at the head), Br.;
to carry away, RV.;
to trace out, discover, investigate, Mn.; MBh.;
 (with अन्यथा) to explain otherwise, Śaṃk. :
Caus. -णाययति, to pass or spend (time), MBh.;
 (also णापयति), to cause a man to marry a woman (acc.), Pañcad.
